<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n90930" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πρωτεσί-λᾱος</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῐ], ὁ</span>, 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πρωτέσι-λας</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <i><span class="en">
			Pi.
			<u>I.</u>
			1.58
		</span></i>; 
			Ion.
		 and 
			Att.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πρωτεσι-λέως</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εω</span>:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>First of the people</i>, name of the hero who
				<i>first</i> leaped ashore at Troy, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				2.698
			</span></i> (so understood by <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i>, ib.<i><span class="en">
				702
			</span></i>, but the name may be a corruption of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πορθεσίλαος</span>, cf. Cret. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πορθεσίλας</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πορτεσίλας</span>) :—<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πρωτεσιλάειον</span></b> , τό, <i>his monument</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				13.1.31
			</span></i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πρωτεσιλάεια</span></b> ,
				τά, <i>his festival</i>, Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>I.</u>
				1.11
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
